(footprint "XTAL_FA-128_2016_4Pin"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "hand")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Epson FA-128 32 MHz crystal, 2.0 x 1.6 x 0.5 mm, 4-pad. Land pattern is Epson's recommended footprint drawing: 0.95 x 0.85 mm pads on 1.45 mm (X) by 1.15 mm (Y) centres, a 2.40 x 2.00 mm outer envelope. Read the drawing's four callouts by where their arrows land: 1.45 and 1.15 terminate on pad CENTRES (pitches), 0.95 and 0.85 terminate on pad EDGES (pad size). X is the crystal's 2.0 mm axis, matching the external-dimensions top view. Pad 1 is bottom-left, then 2 BR, 3 TR, 4 TL, which is Epson's corner numbering. Pads 1 and 3 are the crystal terminals; pads 2 and 4 are the metal cover and must go to ground. KiCad's generic Crystal_SMD_2016-4Pin_2.0x1.6mm (0.90 x 0.80 pads on 1.40 x 1.10 centres, 2.30 x 1.90 envelope) is within 0.05 mm of this on every dimension and shares the same corner numbering, so it is a valid substitute; this footprint exists only to hold Epson's exact figures.")
	(tags "crystal 32MHz 2016 epson FA-128")
	(attr smd)

